[
    {
        "content": "<p>This question is due to me being summoned by the <code>simpNF</code> linter to adjust my writing of the successor of an ordinal. More or less because of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ordinal.limitRecOn#doc\">docs#Ordinal.limitRecOn</a>, I was using <code>Order.succ o</code> for the successor of an ordinal.  </p>\n<p>However, there is a <code>simp</code> tag on <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Order.succ_eq_add_one#doc\">docs#Order.succ_eq_add_one</a> (consistently with the one on <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.succ_eq_add_one#doc\">docs#Nat.succ_eq_add_one</a> etc.) and my question is whether this tag should really be there or not.</p>",
        "id": 596502049,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1779293810
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If this <code>simp</code> stays, then we should get rid of <code>Order.succ</code> spelling in the <code>Ordinal</code> API.</p>",
        "id": 596506492,
        "sender_full_name": "Yury G. Kudryashov",
        "timestamp": 1779294904
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"214703\">Yury G. Kudryashov</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/why.20is.20Order.2Esucc_eq_add_one.20simp.3F/near/596506492\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If this <code>simp</code> stays, then we should get rid of <code>Order.succ</code> spelling in the <code>Ordinal</code> API.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I believe this refactor is already in-progress, and possibly completed</p>",
        "id": 596507495,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779295167
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Found it: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35553\">#35553</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35741\">#35741</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35844\">#35844</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35853\">#35853</a>, see also <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/17033\">#17033</a></p>",
        "id": 596507980,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779295291
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So to answer the question: because you should write <code>o + 1</code> and not <code>Order.succ o</code></p>",
        "id": 596508176,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779295339
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And lemmas should use <code>add_one</code> in their names?</p>",
        "id": 596519880,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1779298334
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, that's also the convention for <code>Nat</code> (<a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Naming.20convention.3A.20succ.20vs.2E.20add_one/with/537179804\">#mathlib4 &gt; Naming convention: succ vs. add_one</a>)</p>",
        "id": 596521221,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779298635
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Then shouldn't <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=SuccOrder.limitRecOn#doc\">docs#SuccOrder.limitRecOn</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ordinal.limitRecOn#doc\">docs#Ordinal.limitRecOn</a> and similar use <code>add_one</code> as well? somethink like: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- Limit induction on ordinals: if one can prove a property by induction at successor ordinals and</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">at limit ordinals, then it holds for all ordinals.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Note that this is just a special (though sometimes convenient) case of the more general</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">well-founded recursion `WellFoundedLT.fix`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">elab_as_elim</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">limitRecOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">add_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">limit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSuccLimit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">SuccOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">limitRecOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ha</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ha</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq_bot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">limit</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 596561918,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1779309785
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(By the way, the docstring should not talk about “property”, because this works as well for constructions.)</p>",
        "id": 596562052,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1779309827
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"459227\">@Violeta Hernández</span></p>",
        "id": 596569087,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779312327
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've been slowly phasing out <code>Order.succ</code> out of the ordinal API, but I'm just one person. Help welcome!</p>",
